  "method": "AIHC built with aihc build (Nix build of the commit above), one cell at a time on a machine with no other benchmark work; load average 3 to 20 from unrelated processes. Each size was searched by fitting the growth exponent between measurements, then timed as the minimum of five complete process runs after one warm-up, with AIHC_RTS_STATS set as the runner does. Wasm modules were precompiled with wasmtime compile -C cache=n and run with -S cli -S http --allow-precompiled. Artifacts were not stripped. Every checksum was compared with a GHC 9.14.1 build.",
  "notes": {
    "pubgrub-solve": "Os does not build with AIHC at this commit (Lir generation: call arity mismatch for an unboxed worker, GHC.Word.$fNumWord64$c+_unboxed or Main.$mix_unboxed, on native, LLVM and Wasm); Os reuses the O1 instance counts.",
    "juicypixels-jpeg": "AIHC Os builds (native, LLVM and Wasm) decode JPEG data incorrectly at this commit; encoding matches GHC. Os sizes were timed with that wrong output, which is what aihc_checksum records for those cells; Main.hs expects GHC's checksum, so those runs fail until the compiler is fixed.",
    "rasterific-scene": "Size is [canvas side, shape count]. O0 cells and Wasm Os use a 128-pixel canvas, since clearing and hashing a 512-pixel canvas alone takes 0.47 to 1.9 seconds there.",
    "happy-codegen": "Size is the number of grammar families; run time grows faster than linearly."
  },
